9ms)\n✔ every identity publishes a distinct optimized hero image (10.3848ms)\n✔ Questions, Threads and Atlas publish distinct world artwork while preserving native destinations (5.8828ms)\n✔ initial HTML requests only the active world; inactive artwork remains in the admitted runtime data (3.4822ms)\n✔ the independent illustrated atlas preserves all forty destinations and return paths (42.9782ms)\n✔ source ownership switches only after ordered module and lowering correspondence, then validation (11.0369ms)\n✔ stale, ambiguous, undeclared and non-corresponding migrations cannot stage (20.1673ms)\n✔ all six retained predecessors pass the actual authoring algebra, shared frontend and whole-module lowerer (22089.3497ms)\n✔ acceptance matches command identity, count, exit status and error rather than PASS strings or ok flags (16.6116ms)\n✔ retirement preserves exact helper bytes before deletion and ignores logs/directories (1.1689ms)\n✔ archive collisions refuse retirement and source switching before validation (2.2837ms)\n✔ clean verification requires a clean revision and absent build, installed dependencies and generated output (1.0407ms)\n✔ normal verification has no .build input and does not rewrite presentation evidence (293.6286ms)\n✔ snapshot comparison hashes binary input bytes and distinguishes an absent creation target (10.1265ms)\n✔ retired helpers remain hashed evidence with no active executable counterpart (315.9536ms)\n✔ the authoring policy admits with only its declared generic mechanisms (310.9774ms)\n✔ previews validate without committing; apply commits the validated proposal before its receipt (4.2696ms)\n✔ bad authority, stale and repeated edits, no-ops and malformed proposals refuse before staging (3.7852ms)\n✔ failed publication validation cannot reach the commit effect (1.103ms)\n✔ all build source owners remain editable; generator predecessors are inert and byte-identical (496.5182ms)\n✔ encounter: exact ordered JSON, whole lowered module and all o