 with independent accessibility and internationalisation sagas (12.7334ms)\n✔ assurance levels require complete cumulative and correctly scoped evidence (56.2205ms)\n✔ entry markup evidence detects missing language, skip targets and image alternatives (138.2403ms)\n✔ portfolio evidence cannot promote partial, duplicated or empty route coverage (567.1263ms)\n✔ fixed-order escaping preserves the predecessor for text, markup and nonstring values (16.3749ms)\n✔ complete element serialization keeps attributes and text escaped with less work (6.2259ms)\n✔ serialization still refuses event handlers and executable URL schemes (2.0097ms)\n✔ SHA-256 fallback agrees with Web Crypto for Unicode and padding boundaries (20.6546ms)\n✔ Temple Merkle drawing geometry, order, labels and fresh highlights match original SVG effects (296ms)\n✔ Temple explanatory lessons match every preset, identity and refusal branch in the source (568.2006ms)\n✔ Sourcery flood scatter, waves and broom poses match original motion at sampled frames (175.7161ms)\n✔ Temple sky scatter, twinkle, parallax, motes and respawn match original canvas effects (218.5999ms)\n✔ Temple constellation geometry, glow, sparks and rings match original canvas effects (80.0416ms)\n✔ reduced motion and hidden documents draw still frames without scheduling animation (8.3494ms)\n✔ film seeking preserves range endpoints and the metadata/blob fallback sequence (3.6438ms)\n✔ Temple genesis identities, canonical bytes, state roots and Merkle levels match the original (76.6236ms)\n✔ every preset, identity and false-root choice reproduces the original proposal, verdict and witness (2814.4383ms)\n✔ amendment, refusals, stale basis, replay and both forgeries preserve the exact history boundary (831.1957ms)\n✔ Sourcery intent classification and all proposal templates match the original source (1332.1498ms)\n✔ Sourcery sealing, returns, witness verification, tampering and restoration match the original (67.3665ms)\n✔ microsite-lamp: ordered surface, complete lowering and original-coordinate coverage agree (15793.8315ms)\n✔ microsite-motion: ordered surface, complete lowering and original-coordinate coverage agree (443.6476ms)\n✔ microsite-temple-motion: ordered surface, complete lowering and original-coordinate coverage agree (796.4246ms)\n✔ microsite-media: ordered surface, complete lowering and original-coordinate coverage agree (288.8315ms)\n✔ batch frontends link against the supplied main closure and refuse foreign profiles and effects (4275.3425ms)\n✔ empty catch bodies are profile-gated; empty try bodies and malformed indentation still refuse (1374.0376ms)\n✔ ownership is singular and every selected readable module has a source-bound Inspect page (2626.9147ms)\n✔ Inspect uses exact authored slices and refuses stale or undeclared source bindings without executing them (3335.9812ms)\n✔ microsite-projection: ordered module, whole lowering and exact source coordinates correspond (6755.2685ms)\n✔ microsites: ordered module, whole lowering and exact source coordinates correspond (211.9349ms)\n✔ microsite-return: ordered module, whole lowering and exact source coordinates correspond (589.5967ms)\n✔ publication profiles use the existing fact operators and link against the same main closure (1252.396ms)\n✔ the owner switch is explicit and each accepted source is visible through the existing Inspect catalogue (150.1459ms)\n✔ Inspect renders publication effects as source, never invokes them, and refuses stale source or undeclared owners (4930.8543ms)\n✔ all four recomposed documents retain their independently compared source structure and reading (415.1196ms)\n✔ microsite navigation and referenced resources stay inside the ecosystem and resolve, including fragments (62.1926ms)\n✔ every captured microsite asset and both complete stylesheets retain their exact bytes (530.3999ms)\n✔ original application JavaScript is an oracle only; shipping behaviour is algebra-owned (56.0834ms)\n✔ every project microsite has exactly one algebra-owned return to the main catalogue (11.5085ms)\n✔ whole-module source compiles to exact ordered JSON with no profile or implicit entrypoint (5257.0704ms)\n✔ every actual statement has an original-coordinate source origin (14.5002ms)\n✔ the entire lowered module is identical through the existing lowerer (1195.0296ms)\n✔ JSON and readable-source legs agree on real documents, formatting, faults and ordered effects (3646.4446ms)\n✔ the successor changes only the declared lexer separator and safe record-key formatting (34.055ms)\n✔ malformed control syntax, unsafe names, unknown operators and mismatched profile refuse (140.4332ms)\n✔ compiler identity refuses changed dependencies before compilation (3.3457ms)\n✔ linking traverses folds and error handlers and refuses undeclared calls or effects (71.2997ms)\n✔ a readable source edit changes execution through the existing lowerer and kernel (78.9833ms)\n✔ the authority switch selects Encounter exclusively and binds generated JSON to its source hash (3.8571ms)\n✔ Inspect displays exact authored characters using compiler ranges rather than regenerated notation (1743.2301ms)\n✔ all bundled research sources preserve their recorded bytes (60.3936ms)\n✔ static entry points and module imports remain relative to their publication path (291.0537ms)\n✔ migrated finite models reproduce every slider setting and bit pattern (59.3543ms)\n✔ both numerical memory trajectories and all plotted coordinates retain exact predecessor results (92.5089ms)\n✔ algebra-owned workshop sessions reproduce source edits, overlays, generated HTML and refusal boundaries (6124.3982ms)\n✔ forty activity source documents retain controls and contain no executable source (0.6065ms)\n✔ the published execution graph contains only admitted bundles and generic native mechanisms (320.7966ms)\n✔ whole-bundle auditing rejects extra executable code and altered native mechanisms (9.631ms)\n✔ document observation executes supplied transformation plans without reader defaults (0.8144ms)\n✔ frame capability choice comes from algebra within the native script-free ceiling (29.6855ms)\n✔ household algebra preserves all 100 authored orientation/change/history trajectories (12511.6566ms)\n✔ household example has full Field chrome, accessible controls, linked claims and admitted runtime (2.3252ms)\n✔ household GoG projection keeps common scales, discrete observations and exact selected data (3.0233ms)\n✔ chart markers include custom temporal inputs, deduplicate changes and exclude whole-run rates (1.0743ms)\n✔ every stop has an authored reading and every offered term has a definition (2.6407ms)\n✔ all sources have a plain introduction while original research and full source notes remain available (43.3243ms)\n✔ rate cards explain the same reported values as rounded percentages (0.8612ms)\n✔ all stylesheet trees reproduce their outputs and keep captured comparison bytes intact (414.2213ms)\n✔ editing a structured declaration changes its projection (0.7244ms)\n✔ unknown or opaque stylesheet nodes are refused rather than copied as raw CSS (4.0329ms)\n✔ the catalogue owns stylesheet and inline routing, and an unsupported catalogue is refused (38.0636ms)\n✔ omitted formatting fields retain the same CSS meaning (1.0261ms)\n✔ every published stylesheet has an algebra owner and no captured CSS is an active build input (9.3593ms)\n✔ inline artwork styles are projected by algebra with exact correspondence for the captured source version (82.1898ms)\n✔ reader and workshop document templates cannot introduce raw CSS blocks or attributes (14.2824ms)\n✔ inline declaration edits use HTML attribute escaping (26.1895ms)\n✔ the published activity runtime receives fully projected artwork rather than CSS placeholders (24.8462ms)\n✔ the historical workshop oracle preserves its exact kernel and native function bodies (8.31ms)\n✔ workshop is a connected tour stop with real static resources (1.1421ms)\n✔ all unaffected scenes retain the captured content of the other changes (23.3277ms)\n▶ portable engine preserves source/overlay ownership and unchanged-state refusals\n  ✔ starts from the checked fixture (0.3181ms)\n  ✔ source edit updates page and row, preserving overlay (0.369ms)\n  ✔ overlay edits its literal and escapes generated markup (0.3705ms)\n  ✔ refuse /EC-T007/ (694.8039ms)\n  ✔ refuse /EC-E010/ (80.2753ms)\n  ✔ refuse /LAB-E001/ (0.6817ms)\n  ✔ stale basis refuses (0.7543ms)\n  ✔ original fixture is unchanged (2.1589ms)\n  ✔ new session starts independently (958.2638ms)\n✔ portable engine preserves source/overlay ownership and unchanged-state refusals (5297.0535ms)\n✔ portable execution agrees with direct native fixture execution for the same edits (8415.5793ms)\nℹ tests 208\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 208\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\nℹ duration_ms 128503.9642\n")
